---
// The shortest honest privacy policy: the app collects nothing, and the page
// says what the parts that do touch the network actually do.
const title = "Basaltty — Privacy";
const updated = "13 September 2026";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Basaltty collects nothing." />
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Syne:wght@400;600&family=Young+Serif&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 12vh 6vw 14vh;
        background: #04060a;
        color: #e2f4fb;
        font-family: Syne, ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.65;
      }
      main { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }
      h1 { font-family: "Young Serif", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 2.4rem; margin: 0 0 0.4em; }
      h2 { font-family: "Young Serif", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2.2em 0 0.4em; }
      p, li { color: rgba(226, 244, 251, 0.78); }
      a { color: #5fddf2; }
      .updated { color: rgba(226, 244, 251, 0.45); font-size: 0.9rem; }
      .back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 3rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        Basaltty collects nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no
        tracking, and no server of ours for anything to be sent to.
      </p>

      <h2>Your terminals</h2>
      <p>
        What your terminals show travels directly between your own devices, over
        a connection encrypted end to end. It does not pass through us, and
        there is nowhere for us to keep it.
      </p>

      <h2>How the devices find each other</h2>
      <p>
        Through your own private iCloud database, which only you can read — not
        us, and not Apple. It holds the name of each device and a few connection
        messages, and the messages are deleted a second later, as soon as the
        connection is made.
      </p>

      <h2>Naming your tabs</h2>
      <p>
        The names and groups are worked out by a model running on your Mac.
        Nothing about your tabs leaves the machine they are on.
      </p>

      <h2>Buying Basaltty Pro</h2>
      <p>
        Purchases are handled by Apple. We never see your payment details, and
        Apple does not give them to us. Whether a subscription is active is
        stored in your own private iCloud database so that your Mac can check
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Basaltty is not directed at children and collects nothing from anybody.</p>

      <h2>Asking about this</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/FezVrasta/basaltty/issues">github.com/FezVrasta/basaltty</a>.
      </p>

      <a class="back" href=".">Back to Basaltty</a>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
